<title>UK: UK's Blair says has only a few Labour Euro rebels.</title>
<headline>UK's Blair says has only a few Labour Euro rebels.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Labour Party leader Tony Blair said on Thursday that there were only a handful of anti-Europeans rebels in his party, in stark contrast to the ruling Conservatives.</p>
<p>&quot;You've got one or two Labour people who have always been anti-Common Market and they'll carry on. It's not a big deal,&quot; Blair told a news conference. &quot;We have no situation where shadow ministers are defying the party's manifesto.&quot;</p>
</text>
